 [[File:E 549.png|thumb|[[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gory]], the first example of a Behemoth]]
'''Behemoth Enemies''' (超獣 ''Chōjū'', '''Super-Beasts''') are a type of enemy introduced in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]] and mainly encountered in the [[Empress' Research|Empress' Excavation]] and [[Behemoth Culling]] stages, late [[Uncanny Legends]], [[Zero Legends]], [[Otherworld Colosseum]] and the [[Zombie Outbreaks]] of [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapters 2 and 3. Behemoths tend to have at least one immunity (most commonly to [[Surge Attack|Surges]]), very high stats compared to most regular enemies, and special attack types such as Long Distance, Omni Strike, or Multi-Hit.

The only ability to specifically affect Behemoths is [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer]], which increases damage against them to 2.5x, reduces damage taken from them to 0.6x and provides a set chance to dodge their attacks.

Like [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] and [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin]], Behemoth always overlaps with one of the standard enemy types. Design-wise, Behemoths tend to be more feral or monstrous-looking compared to their other variants.

