|[[Ragin' Gory]]
|[[Wikia:monsterhunter:Blango|Blango]]
|Ragin' Gory is not overtly similar to any monster in particular, but might represent Blango, a highly aggressive, simian [[wikia:monsterhunter:Fanged Beast|Fanged Beast]] with the opposite fur color to Ragin' Gory (white instead of black). Unlike most other Behemoths, Ragin' Gory is a peon that often spawns in groups, just as Blango is a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Category:Small Monsters|Small Monster]] that hunts in packs. His Japanese name (怒りのブラッゴリ ''Ikari no Buraggori'') shares ブラ ''Bura'' (Bla) and ゴ ''go'' with Blango (ブランゴ ''Burango''), though ブラッゴリ ''Buraggori'' is just [[Gory Dark]]'s Japanese name.<br>Ragin' Gory could also simply be the only Behemoth that doesn't reference ''Monster Hunter'' in any way, as he was added over a year before the Behemoth type.
|-
|[[Ultima Beast Naala]]
|[[Wikia:monsterhunter:Kirin|Kirin]]
|Naala mainly appears to be based on the unicorn-like [[wikipedia:Qilin|qilin/kirin]] from Chinese mythology, but its ability to rapidly call down series of lightning bolts is very similar to ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s Kirin in particular.
|-
|[[Wild Doge]]
|[[Wikia:monsterhunter:Canyne|Canyne]]
|Similar ears and cheek fur, with the same X-shaped marking on his forehead.
|-
