*Ensanglion the Calamity's Japanese description refers to him as an ancient/elder dragon (古龍 ''koryū''), while [[Pterowl Hazuku]]'s Japanese name (超竜獣オウルハズク'' Chō Ryūjū Ōruhazuku'') translates to "Super Dragon-Beast Owlhazuku", but they use different kanji for "dragon": Ensanglion's is 龍, whereas Hazuku's is 竜. In ''Monster Hunter'' terms, Ensanglion is an [[Wikia:monsterhunter:Elder Dragon|Elder Dragon]] (古龍種 ''Koryūshu''), but Hazuku is only a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Flying Wyvern|Flying Wyvern]] (飛竜種 ''Hiryūshu'') or [[wikia:monsterhunter:Bird Wyvern|Bird Wyvern]] (鳥竜種 ''Chōryūshu'').
*Lophiiformes Angaburu is the only Behemoth to have no immunities.
*[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] is the only trait without any Behemoths.
*Ragin' Gory, Ultima Beast Naala and Wild Doge existed before the Behemoth type itself; they were retroactively given the type in version 11.5.
*Most of the Behemoths were exclusive to the Behemoth Culling, Hunter's Map and/or [[Empress' Research|Empress' Excavation]] stages before appearing in [[Uncanny Legends]], [[Legend Stages|Zero Legends]] or the [[Catclaw Championships]].
*Despite his name, [[Le'Behemoth]] is not a Behemoth enemy. This is a [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]-specific discrepancy caused by poor localization: the Behemoth type's Japanese name is "Super Beast" (超獣 ''Chōjū''), which is distinct from the "Behemoth" part of Le'Behemoth's Japanese name.
*[[Behemoth's Peak]]'s English name may have been intended to foreshadow the addition of the Behemoth type, beginning with the general introduction of Ultima Beast Naala.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 12.6 Update|12.6]], the syntax used for Behemoth's traits in the [[Enemy Guide]] was more inconsistent: Ragin' Gory, Ultima Beast Naala, Wild Doge, Casaurian Ahirujo, Pterowl Hazuku, Crustaceous Scissorex, Suidae Piggicus and Iguanidae Ibilujon were listed as "(Trait / Behemoth)", Lophiiformes Angaburu was already "(Zombie/Floating/Behemoth)" like it is now, with no spaces between the slashes, and all other Behemoths were listed as "(Trait) (Behemoth)".
